& [ImplementationUnit] is one safe pure Rust module
  + [forms_profile] is cantor-phase3-topology-forms/0.2
  + [receipt_profile] is cantor-phase3-topology-receipt/0.2
  + [scanner_profile] is cantor-windows-candidate-topology/0.1
  + [crate] is cantor_ecosystem
  + [module] is topology_forms
  + [dependencies] is existing serde and serde_json only
  - never: import fs, os, process, net, time, env, random, key, database, provider, model, or unsafe facilities

& [ProfileSeparation] is mandatory
  + [forms_profile] identifies the complete pure machine-form vocabulary
  + [receipt_profile] identifies the serialized TopologyReceipt contract
  + [scanner_profile] identifies the physical observation policy a future producer claims
  + [SJS_protocol] identifies specification processing and equals ad10f10f-d506-48ef-a805-f8b0a133766c
  - never: accept one profile value in another profile field

& [Limits] are positive and capped
  + [maximum_entries] is 1 through 1000000
  + [maximum_depth] is 1 through 256
  + [maximum_path_bytes] is 1 through 32768
  + [maximum_file_bytes] is 1 through 1099511627776
  + [maximum_total_bytes] is 1 through 4398046511104
  + [maximum_streams_per_entry] is 1 through 1024
  + [deadline_tick] is nonzero
  = must: maximum_file_bytes cannot exceed maximum_total_bytes

& [StrongFileIdentity] is exact
  + [volume_serial] is unsigned 64-bit
  + [file_id_hex] is exactly 32 lowercase hexadecimal characters
  + [scope] is caller-owned and scan-local

& [StreamFact] is coherent
  + [name] is nonempty, NUL-free, and at most 1024 bytes
  + [size] is unsigned 64-bit
  + [kind] is unnamed_default or named_data
  + [unnamed_default] requires name ::$DATA
  + [named_data] rejects name ::$DATA

& [EntryObservation] is structurally coherent
  + [kind] is root_directory, directory, or regular_file
  + [relative_path] is absent exactly for root_directory
  + [descendant_path] is canonical, at most 32768 bytes, and excludes empty, dot, dot-dot, colon, backslash, NUL, and .git segments
  + [mode_class] is directory, regular_non_executable, or regular_executable and matches kind
  + [attributes] is caller-observed u32 without policy interpretation
  + [identity] is required
  + [number_of_links] is nonzero
  + [streams] are sorted by name, unique, at most 1024, and contain at most one unnamed_default
  + [length] and [content_sha256] are present exactly for regular_file
  + [observation_ordinal] is caller-owned and nonzero
  - never: interpret a valid observation form as an admitted entry

& [Receipt] is a fresh content-addressed claim with explicit root binding
  + [receipt_profile] equals cantor-phase3-topology-receipt/0.2
  + [scanner_profile] equals cantor-windows-candidate-topology/0.1
  + [candidate_root] is nonempty, NUL-free, and at most 32768 bytes while physical canonicality remains M2C responsibility
  + [root_identity] is a valid StrongFileIdentity
  + [root_volume_guid_path] is valid canonical syntax under VolumeGuidPath
  + [admission_profile] is nonempty, NUL-free, and at most 128 bytes
  + [admission_receipt_sha256] and [policy_sha256] and [ordered_inventory_sha256] are canonical SHA-256
  + [scan_nonce] is nonempty, NUL-free, and at most 256 bytes
  + [entry_count] is nonzero and within limits
  + [total_file_bytes] is within limits
  + [consistency] is quiescent_double_inventory only
  + [issued_tick] is less than [expires_tick]
  + [expires_tick] is less than or equal to the bound scan deadline tick
  - never: claim form validity proves candidate_root, root_identity, and root_volume_guid_path correspond physically

& [VolumeGuidPath] is strict syntax
  + [prefix] is exactly \\?\Volume{
  + [GUID] is exactly 8-4-4-4-12 lowercase ASCII hexadecimal
  + [root_suffix] is exactly }\
  + [tail] is absent or one or more backslash-separated components
  + [component] is nonempty, NUL-free, contains no forward slash, and is neither dot nor dot-dot
  + [tail_case] is preserved exactly
  + [maximum] is 32768 UTF-8 bytes
  - never: accept DOS, UNC, device, NT, relative, uppercase-GUID, malformed-GUID, empty-component, dot-component, NUL, or over-bound forms
  - never: claim syntax proves path existence, locality, filesystem type, or identity equality

& [LegacyPolicy] is reject
  + [old_field] is profile
  + [old_missing_fields] are receipt_profile, scanner_profile, root_identity, and root_volume_guid_path
  + [decoder] is strict deny-unknown-field JSON with no defaults
  + [migration] is none because no scanner, persisted receipt, ledger, or external consumer exists
  - never: synthesize missing physical evidence or retain an implicit legacy path

& [Consumption] is immutable use evidence
  + [topology_receipt_sha256] and [mutation_work_packet_sha256] are canonical SHA-256
  + [issued_tick] is less than or equal to [consumed_tick]
  + [consumed_tick] is strictly less than [expires_tick]
  - never: claim the pure form enforces global uniqueness; the future supervisor ledger must do so

& [RuntimeFault] is honest
  + [operation] is validate_request, enumerate_directory, open_entry, query_attributes, query_identity, query_links, enumerate_streams, read_content, repeat_inventory, or issue_receipt
  + [class] is invalid_request, limit, path, reparse, hard_link, duplicate_identity, stream, attribute, special_entry, Git_topology, unsupported_platform, access, not_found, changed_during_scan, or other_OS
  + [relative_path] when present obeys descendant path rules
  + [os_error] is optional signed 32-bit evidence
  + [may_have_changed] true requires quarantine_candidate
  + [changed_during_scan] requires may_have_changed true and quarantine_candidate
  + [deny_launch] requires may_have_changed false

& [InheritedRequirementSet] is P3TF-001 through P3TF-010
  + [P3TF-001] is strict JSON and bounded faults
  + [P3TF-002] is hard positive scan limits
  + [P3TF-003] is canonical strong identity
  + [P3TF-004] is coherent entry and content evidence
  + [P3TF-005] is sorted unique bounded stream evidence
  + [P3TF-006] is canonical root-versus-descendant path semantics
  + [P3TF-007] is complete receipt binding and honest consistency
  + [P3TF-008] is in-range immutable consumption evidence
  + [P3TF-009] is honest runtime-fault consequence
  + [P3TF-010] is no effect surface plus global verification and rollback

& [RevisionRequirementSet] is P3TR-001 through P3TR-012
  + [P3TR-001] is exact multi-source preservation and lineage
  + [P3TR-002] is honest prior-signature invalidation
  + [P3TR-003] is forms profile 0.2
  + [P3TR-004] is receipt profile 0.2
  + [P3TR-005] is separate scanner profile 0.1
  + [P3TR-006] is required strong root identity
  + [P3TR-007] is canonical bounded volume-GUID path syntax
  + [P3TR-008] is preservation of predecessor receipt invariants
  + [P3TR-009] is strict fail-closed legacy and malformed-input rejection
  + [P3TR-010] is unchanged pure no-effect boundary
  + [P3TR-011] is focused/global proof, evidence, and rollback
  + [P3TR-012] is valid SJS signature and complete registry lineage

& [Acceptance] is exact
  + [schema] old JSON rejects and new valid JSON round-trips exactly
  + [profiles] substitution and unknown values reject independently
  + [identity] missing and malformed root identity reject
  + [path] every grammar boundary has positive and negative tests
  + [regression] all prior M2A tests and global workspace gates pass
  + [purity] dependency set, imports, unsafe count, and effect surface do not expand
  + [evidence] clone-portable manifest binds current source, specification, code, tests, solution, and proof

& [ImplementationBoundary] is pure schema revision only
  + [allowed] is constants, fields, pure validation, pure tests, documentation, evidence, proof, and rollback
  + [forbidden] is dependency change, unsafe, Windows API, filesystem, clock, random, environment, persistence, process, network, model, scanner execution, fixture, sandbox, mutation, seal, cleanup, and promotion

& [SJSProcessingTrace] is complete
  + [source_preserved] is correction source plus byte-identical pre-revision snapshot
  + [delineated] is four identity domains and syntax-versus-truth boundary
  + [exploded] is twelve atomic revision requirements and eight failure modes
  + [semantically_refined] is exact field, grammar, role, authority, and compatibility meaning
  + [constraint_checked] is ten-source-grounded constraints with the prior signature conflict repaired
  + [pruned] is legacy upgrade, physical I/O, Unicode normalization, scanner version change, and Windows dependency growth
  + [data_design_checked] is conceptual observation, logical receipt, physical JSON, projection lineage, and rescan invalidation
  + [exhaustion_reviewed] is seven_fold_phase_locked
  + [justified] is explicit safety, compatibility, timing, tradeoff, and rollback rationale
  + [registry_recorded] is all durable nodes and lineage edges

& [SignatureEvidenceTable] binds every claimed stage
  + [source_preserved] is SJS_Reprocessing_Input_Manifest.sop with exact hashes and byte-equality record
  + [delineated] is exploded specification BoundaryFormation and TruthBoundary
  + [exploded] is the separate Cantor_Phase3_Topology_Receipt_Root_Binding_Revision.exploded.sop
  + [semantically_refined] is exploded specification SemanticRefinementTrace
  + [constraint_checked] is exploded specification ConstraintLedger and ConstraintCheckTrace
  + [pruned] is exploded specification PruningTrace
  + [seven_fold_phase_locked] is exploded specification FoldTrace and ExhaustionReview
  + [data_design_checked] is exploded specification DataDesignModel and DataDesignQualityGate
  + [justified] is justification PrimaryClaim, support anchors, confidence, Counterarguments, and InvalidationConditions
  + [planned] is Cantor_Phase3_Topology_Receipt_Root_Binding_Revision_Plan.sop
  + [registry_recorded] is Cantor_Phase3_Topology_Receipt_Root_Binding_Revision_Registry.sop

